  "tagline": "The standard Postgres extension for vector similarity search with HNSW and IVFFlat indexes.",
  "description": "pgvector adds a vector type plus halfvec, bit and sparsevec variants to PostgreSQL, with exact search and approximate HNSW and IVFFlat indexes, so embeddings live in the same rows, transactions and backups as the rest of your data. It is available on essentially every managed Postgres (RDS, Aurora, Cloud SQL, AlloyDB, Azure, Supabase, Neon), which makes it the lowest-friction way to add semantic search to an existing app. Iterative index scans (0.8) fixed the worst filtered-query recall problems. It is comfortable into the tens of millions of vectors; beyond that, index build memory and filtering trade-offs push teams toward pgvectorscale, VectorChord or a dedicated vector database.",
